"""Register the BeamDrill shouldConsume gate (N2202).

N2155 gave the beam drill its live power.status read (a pure
power row over the stamped frame value, folded by the shared
machinery into the min efficiency, BuildingComp.java:1969-1976,
ConsumePower.efficiency is build.power.status) -- but RED-deferred
the shouldConsume gate: the port tracked NO items or facing state
on any placed-beam-drill frame, so the machinery ran with
should_consume=true when enabled -- a plasma-bore with a full
item store, or facing no wall ore at all, drilled as if
power.status were 1.0 while Java efficiency is 0. N2202 resolves
that deferral. BeamDrillBuild.shouldConsume (BeamDrill.java:270-271,
`return items.total() < itemCapacity && facingAmount > 0 && enabled;`)
is a three-way conjunction: the item store under capacity, at least
one facing wall-ore tile, and enabled. BeamDrill extends Block
(BeamDrill.java:25, `public class BeamDrill extends Block{`), NOT
Drill, and BeamDrillBuild extends Building (BeamDrill.java:220,
`public class BeamDrillBuild extends Building{`), so the gate lives
on the beam-drill family's OWN driver (SourceBeamDrillBuildState.gd,
frame key "source_beam_drill_building"), not the drill frame.

facingAmount is a plain int field (BeamDrill.java:228, `public int
facingAmount;`, Java default 0), recomputed by updateFacing()
(BeamDrill.java:375-410, called from updateTile :244 and
onProximityUpdate :365): for each of the size facing lasers it walks
range tiles along the rotation, takes the first solid tile, and
counts it when its wallDrop is mineable (`facingAmount = 0;` then
`facingAmount ++;` per mineable facing tile, BeamDrill.java:379/:392).
updateConsumption runs BEFORE updateTile (BuildingComp.java:2274-2277),
so the gate reads the previous tick's facingAmount -- correct per
Java, NOT a bug. The live facing scan waits for its own slice (the
facing/laser binding deferral stays -- the port HAS the tile infra
to compute it later: game.source_world_tile + tile_wall_drop_state +
the catalog tier/range/size, so this is deferred work, not a
blocker); this slice adds the frame key (Java default 0) and the pure
gate over it, and the driver feeds the gate to the machinery.
itemCapacity comes from the catalog (block.properties["itemCapacity"]):
10 for plasma-bore (the Block.java:75 field default, `public int
itemCapacity = 10;`) and 20 for large-plasma-bore (Blocks.java:3062,
`itemCapacity = 20;`). The items total reuses the drill inventory
helper (SourceDrillInventoryRuntimeState.items_total over the frame
items Dictionary, the Building.items ItemModule, the factory
precedent); the production advance that fills the store
(BeamDrill.java:253-261) waits for its own slice, so the gate reads
the current frame. When the gate is false, updateConsumption forces
efficiency to zero (BuildingComp.java:1960 + 1992).

Composition, not re-implementation: the shared efficiency machinery
(SourceBuildingEfficiencyState.update_consumption_state) already folds
should_consume=false into efficiency 0 via the update gate
(BuildingComp.java:1960 + 1992). N2202 does not touch it. N2202
supplies the missing pure gate (source_beam_drill_should_consume_state)
+ the frame items/facing_amount keys + the driver wiring; no new
consumer rows. Three result symbols: the gate, the items total it
reads, and the facing amount it reads.

Shard note: the production shards DO select this slice --
production_slices selects ledger entries whose java_source contains
/world/blocks/production/ (BeamDrill.java qualifies; N2155 is already
there), so production_slices / production_symbols /
production_api_contracts / production_state_schema all gain the N2202
entries when this register runs. No other shard changes.
"""

